CATEGORIES:Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Discover how source-grounded AI differs from LLMs like\, ChatG
 PT\, Claude and Gemini\nIn this brief introduction to Gemini Notebook\, y
 ou’ll learn how to upload a variety of sources\, analyze dense scholarly 
 articles\, and chat directly with your personal research. It uses your ex
 act source citations\, thus reducing those troublesome AI hallucinations.
 \nWe'll also explore the Studio to turn your Notebook into: study tools\,
  detailed reports\, beautiful slide presentations\, infographics and vide
 os. Gemini Notebook can also aggregate\, cross reference\, extract data a
 nd identify key findings from your uploaded sources.\nRegister Here: http
 s://montclair.libcal.com/event/18025135\n\nHosted by: Sprague Library\n\n
 Additional Information can be found at: https://montclair.campuslabs.com/
 engage/event/12986749
DTEND:20261130T161500Z
DTSTAMP:20261128T073028Z
DTSTART:20261130T153000Z
LOCATION:Sprague Library Instruction Room 203
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Gemini Notebook: your AI research assistant
UID:https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12986749
URL:https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12986749
X-HOSTS:Sprague Library
