BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Montclair State University
CATEGORIES:ThoughtfulLearning
CATEGORIES:Academic/Educational/Intellectual
DESCRIPTION:Perspectives on Human Trafficking: Office of the New Jersey At
 torney General\nJoin the Global Center on Human Trafficking (GCHT) at Mon
 tclair State University for two upcoming presentations featuring represen
 tatives from the New Jersey Office of the Attorney General. These session
 s will explore human trafficking in New Jersey\, including victim-centere
 d responses\, online exploitation\, and emerging challenges for law enfor
 cement.\nBoth events are free and open to all\, with options to attend in
  person or virtually.\nNovember 18\, 2026 | Sexual Violence Unit\nTime: 3
 :45 PM – 5:00 PMLocation: Calcia Hall\, Room 140Presenter: Kathleen Fries
 s\, Program & Training Coordinator\, Office of the New Jersey Attorney Ge
 neral\nDrawing on more than 20 years of experience in the field\, Kathlee
 n Friess will provide an overview of human trafficking in New Jersey\, in
 cluding how to recognize potential indicators\, understand vulnerabilitie
 s\, and respond appropriately.\nThe presentation will also highlight New 
 Jersey's efforts to address human trafficking through a victim-centered\,
  trauma-informed approach.\nNovember 30\, 2026 | Cyber Bureaus\nTime: 12:
 00 PM – 1:20 PMLocation: Calcia Hall\, Room 140Presenter: Laura Magnone\,
  Bureau Chief of the Human Trafficking and Cyber Bureaus\, Office of the 
 New Jersey Attorney General\nJoin Laura Magnone for a presentation explor
 ing online exploitation from a legal and law enforcement perspective\, in
 cluding approaches to investigation and prosecution\, and emerging challe
 nges facing the field.\n\nHosted by: College of Humanities and Social Sci
 ences (CHSS)\, Global Center on Human Trafficking\n\nAdditional Informati
 on can be found at: https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/1298602
 8
DTEND:20261130T183000Z
DTSTAMP:20261128T073028Z
DTSTART:20261130T170000Z
LOCATION:Calcia Hall\, 140
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Perspectives on Human Trafficking Series: Office of the Attorney G
 eneral
UID:https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12986028
URL:https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12986028
X-HOSTS:Global Center on Human Trafficking
END:VEVENT
