CATEGORIES:CommunityService
CATEGORIES:Service
DESCRIPTION: \nJoin our weekly Food Recovery events\, where dedicated volu
 nteers and members gather to make a difference in our community. Each wee
 k\, participants help collect perfectly good leftover food from Gourmet D
 ining and transport it to Blanton. There\, the food is repackaged into in
 dividual microwavable containers and stocked in the food pantry\, providi
 ng meals for those in need throughout the week. \nTo Participate: RSVP to
  attend the event each week. Meet in Blanton Hall Residence Hall Kitchene
 tte in the Communal Area (Tell them you are working with Food Recovery)\,
  Sign in via Event Pass and your set!\nRequirements:\n\nVolunteers must b
 e Food Safe Certified to participate.\nComplete the certification by foll
 owing the step-by-step instructions provided in this link.\nOnce certifie
 d\, email your certification to foodrecoverynetwork@sgamsu.org to confirm
  your eligibility to participate.\n\nYour involvement helps reduce food w
 aste and insecurity while supporting individuals in our community who are
  in need. We look forward to your participation!*Please Note: This event 
 end time is dependent on the amount of food given. You can estimate for m
 ax of hour and a half for recoveries.\n\nHosted by: EATS by Gourmet Dinin
 g\, Food Recovery Network\, Red Hawk Pantry\n\nAdditional Information can
  be found at: https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12999310
